:: Jackson Hang Out End Late High Fun [nobr]

/* Intro */
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> is bouncing up and down, following behind you as he rambles off about whatever recent thing you did or game you played. <span style="color:LightGreen">He’s been making his enjoyment of the day clear, and you can’t help but chuckle at his enthusiasm,</span> <span style="color:Yellow">when he suddenly stops in his tracks and you high him sigh loudly.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
        Name: "Player",
        State: {
            Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
        {
        Name: "Jackson",
        State: {
            Outfit: $HangOutClothes,
            Mouth: "Frown",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh man! The sun’s going down already!?”</span> You turn to see his shoulders slump and his face fall at the sight of the dwindling day, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Come on sun, can’t you just stay up a little longer?”</span> The boy pleads, but the sun refuses to budge, and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> puffs out his cheeks in frustration before turning to you. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I gotta go home… Mom says my curfew is sundown and if I’m home late, she’ll beat my butt. Sorry…”</span><br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
	<<link "Ask him to stay out a little longer<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        You ask him to stay out a little longer. A few more games, a couple more minutes. You’re sure it won’t be a big deal, and even if it is, it’ll be worth it! <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span>’s face perks up for a moment, as if he is seriously considering your offer, before he sighs once more. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I really want to… but I can’t. Mom’s still mad at me for spilling juice on her carpet last month. She REALLY likes her carpet. But we can play tomorrow! Okay?”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:LightGreen">You give <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> a smile and a nod, bidding the boy farewell and accepting that the boy’s got to go.</span> You should probably be thinking about heading home soon as well.<br>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Park]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>

	<<link "Give him a hug goodbye<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        You sigh as well, wanting to stay out a little longer but fully accepting that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> has to go. Afterall, if you did stay out a little longer, he could get grounded which would mean less time in the future to hang out! <span style="color:LightGreen">You walk up to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> with a reassuring smile and give him a big hug goodbye, bidding him farewell and promising to hang out again soon.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah! Next time we should go hiking in the woods or play a game in the park or-”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> starts to ramble, though you remind him of his pressing time limit and he chuckles. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh yeah. Bye-bye, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$JacksonNickname</span>! I’ll see you tomorrow!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> turns around and runs off towards his house. You should probably be thinking about heading home soon as well.<br>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Park]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>